 Common Production Issues (Every DevOps/SRE Should Know)🚀 


Working with Docker & Kubernetes in production is not just about deployments  it’s about handling real-world issues under pressure.

Here are advanced, common issues I’ve seen in real production systems, along with what typically causes them and how you troubleshoot them.

Whether you're a DevOps, SRE, Platform Engineer, or preparing for interviews, these scenarios will help you think like a real production engineer. 👇

Docker – Advanced Production Issues

Container running but application not accessible
 Wrong EXPOSE port / host-port mismatch.

High Docker image size causing slow deployments
No multistage build, cache not used.

 “ImagePullBackOff” in Kubernetes
Private registry auth failure or wrong tag.

 Docker daemon high CPU usage
Too many logs, resource leaks, large layers.

 Container keeps restarting
 App crash loop, wrong CMD/ENTRYPOINT.

 Disk full due to unused images
 docker system prune not applied.

 Can't connect container-to-container
 Wrong network mode or misconfigured overlay network.

 Timezone mismatch inside containers
 Container running UTC, app expecting IST.

 Permission denied writing files inside container
Wrong user in Dockerfile (root vs non-root).

 Docker build cache not working
 COPY order issues.

Slow startup due to large dependencies
Heavy base images, unnecessary packages.

 Secrets accidentally baked inside images
 ENV variables hardcoded in Dockerfile.

 Container unable to access external APIs
 DNS issues or network policies.

 Multi-architecture image issues
 amd64 vs arm64 mismatch.

 Docker Swarm node flapping (less common now)
 Gossip failure / overlay network issues.

 Kubernetes – Advanced Production Issues

 CrashLoopBackOff
 Misconfigured env variables, DB unreachable.

 OOMKilled
 Containers hitting memory limits.

 Node Not Ready
 Disk pressure, network plugin failure.

 Pod stuck in Pending state
 No matching node selector / taints & tolerations issue.

 High etcd latency
 Large clusters, huge objects stored.

 DNS resolution failure inside pods
 CoreDNS crash, network plugin issues.

 Services not reachable
 Wrong Service type (ClusterIP/NodePort), missing selectors.

 Horizontal Pod Autoscaler not scaling
 Metrics server not installed, wrong metrics API.

 PVC stuck in Pending
 StorageClass mismatch.

 Pods evicted due to node resource pressure
 MemoryPressure / DiskPressure.

 ImagePullBackOff
 Private registry authentication or incorrect image tag.

 ReadinessProbe failures
 App not ready, wrong probe path.

 NetworkPolicy blocking traffic
 Too restrictive ingress/egress.

 Ingress not routing
 Missing annotations, pathType issues.

 ConfigMap not updating inside running pods
 Pods need restart; volume mounts don’t auto-refresh.
